range bed level 0.14 0.2 a glass drone at C3 and C4: a sine with a quiet, bell-stretched harmonic bank, breathing slowly. Synthesized, so its pitch is exact.
range bed ph_pos 0 1 the phaser notch, parked by the orb's curl (mix fixed at 0.6)
range deep level 0 0.3 the lake under the ice: the aqueous rumble, all but frozen, mostly its noise (sines 0.3) so it adds weight and no notes
range root level 0 0.18 C4 with its octave: bowed glass (sine + stretched bank, slow attack)
range root bank_shimmer 0 0.4 the overtones wander while the reach is wrong (fit)
range root lfo>amp 0 0.6 the tremble: shimmering at coherence 0, perfectly still at 1 (frozen)
range third level 0 0.16 E4
range fifth level 0 0.16 G4
range seventh level 0 0.12 Bb4
range frost level 0 0.35 the frost pad as an accent: every partial pulled onto C and G (gather 1, power chord), so its cluster cannot clash; in with stir
range glass level 0 0.7 the aqueous stream's droplets an octave up, bell-stretched, gathered onto the chord
range glass speed 0.02 0.25 never liquid: slow ice at coherence 0, frozen solid at 1
range creak level 0 0.5 crunching ice as a choir (eight read heads, one pitch): the pen's speed
range creak speed 1.06 2.28
range creak ph_pos 0.01333 1
range wind level 0 0.18 the stream high-passed and slowed: a cold hiss, in with stir
range cloud level 0 0.18 the chord at C5 in sines, growing with the machine; spells raise it and pick the chord
range cloud voices 4 8
range cloud gather 0.6 1
bind stir bed level 0.2 0.14
bind stack bed level 0 -0.04 rel
bind orb.radius bed cutoff 0.5 0.9
bind orb.curl bed ph_pos 0 1
bind stack deep level 0 0.3
bind tone.root root level 0 0.18
bind tone.third third level 0 0.16
bind tone.fifth fifth level 0 0.16
bind tone.seventh seventh level 0 0.12
bind coherence root lfo>amp 0.6 0
bind coherence third lfo>amp 0.6 0
bind coherence fifth lfo>amp 0.6 0
bind coherence seventh lfo>amp 0.6 0
bind fit root bank_shimmer 0.4 0
bind fit third bank_shimmer 0.4 0
bind fit fifth bank_shimmer 0.4 0
bind fit seventh bank_shimmer 0.4 0
bind orb.radius root cutoff 0.55 1
bind orb.radius third cutoff 0.55 1
bind orb.radius fifth cutoff 0.55 1
bind orb.radius seventh cutoff 0.55 1
bind stir frost level 0 0.35
bind orb.radius frost cutoff 0.6 1
bind coherence frost shimmer 0.3 0
bind stack glass level 0 0.7
bind coherence glass speed 0.25 0.02
bind radiance glass reverb 0.6 0.95
bind orb.speed creak level 0 0.5
bind orb.speed creak speed
bind orb.accel creak drive 0.12 0.3
bind orb.radius creak cutoff 0.6 1
bind stir wind level 0 0.18
bind orb.radius wind cutoff 0.65 0.85
bind stack cloud level 0 0.18
bind coherence cloud gather 0.6 1
bind stack cloud voices 4 8
bind orb.curl creak ph_pos
bind hand.fit glass level 0 0.25 rel
note cryic v2 (2026-10-03): everything pitched is made from oscillators, the recordings are texture. (v1 used the frost pad as bed and voices; it is in git history.)
note Why: the frost pad is not a note but a cluster (measured, as tuned: C, D, D#, F#, G#, A, many of them 20-40 cents off), so as v1's bed and all four voices it
note fought every chord the arms made. Here the bed and the voices are sines with a quiet bell-stretched bank (bowed glass, a glass harmonica), exact in pitch;
note the pad returns only as the frost layer, with gather 1 pulling each of its partials onto C or G, at accent level.
note in tune = stillness: the voices tremble (lfo>amp 0.6 -> 0 with coherence) until they freeze, the droplets stop, the frost's shimmer clears; fit steadies the overtones.
note orb = the ice crackle (level and rate) with the pen's speed, filters with its radius, the bed's phaser notch with its curl.
note One-shots: freezing splash on lock, a glass tink on accept, the swish-whip crack on unlock. Spells are placeholders.
note Reach hint: hand.fit (the reach of the component in hand against the recipe the stations point to) adds a little to one layer when it is right, and nothing otherwise; fit steadies the voices.
note Recipes are the sigil generator's (seed 1, 2026-10-03). Spell notes that name ratios or chord tones describe the earlier, hand-made recipes.

